    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "We have used the = operator many times in our code. It's used to assign a value to a variable."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "// assign 3.1415 to the pi variable\ndouble pi = 3.1415;"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Now, let's take a look at other assignment operators."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        [
          "Operator",
          "Example",
          "Equivalent to"
        ],
        [
          "+=",
          "x += 5",
          "x = x + 5"
        ],
        [
          "-=",
          "x -= 5",
          "x = x - 5"
        ],
        [
          "*=",
          "x *= 5",
          "x = x * 5"
        ],
        [
          "/=",
          "x /= 5",
          "x = x / 5"
        ],
        [
          "%=",
          "x %= 5",
          "x = x % 5"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "These assignment operators perform arithmetic and assignment operations at the same time."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
